Mr. Sweta Kumar Dash, Secretary, Cuttack Development Authority is present through virtual mode and has filed an affidavit dated 14.08.2025, wherein it is stated as follows:
(i) The DCP in the letter dated 14.05.2025 addressed to the Vice-Chairman, CDA requested for installation of CCTV Surveillance Camera System at 191 locations of the Cuttack City for monitoring public safety, enhancing law enforcement response, improving traffic management and aiding in the prevention and detection of crime;
(ii) The DCP in another letter dated 14.05.2025 requested for installation of Electronic Traffic Signal System at different places in the Cuttack City;
(iii) The ACP (TR) in letter no.292 dated 25.02.2025, sent a proposal for installation of CCTV in 107 different locations in Cuttack City.

(vi) Thereafter, CDA entered in agreement with the said Company on 17.06.2025, a copy of which has been enclosed as Annexure-B. Consequently, the Company was paid 50% of the consideration i.e., Rs.22,76,95,520/- (rupees twenty two crores seventy six lakhs ninety five thousand five hundred twenty) for CCTV Surveillance camera in 107 locations and Rs.04,09,86,194/- (rupees four crores nine lakhs eighty six thousand one hundred ninety four) towards Traffic Signal System at 30 Registrar (Judicial) vs State Of Odisha & Others .... Opp. ... on 26 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/87422815/
2 locations, in total Rs.26,86,80,714/- (Rupees twenty six crores eighty six lakhs eighty thousand seven hundred fourteen) as advance towards procurement of cameras and other components and for installation/setup in the spot;
(vii) As ascertained, the Company commenced the work in 10 nos. of the locations and in the process to proceed with installation in other different locations;
(viii) In the meanwhile, the DCP, Cuttack in its letter dtd. 14.05.2025, further requested to add additional 84 locations;

The Committees desiring to construct pandal/gate by digging at any location will deposit requisite fee to the CMC and the money receipt be furnished at license cell in the Office of the deponent for considering issuance of license;
(ii) No Objection Certificate pertaining to electric fittings be obtained from the Addl. Chief Engineer -cum- Electrical Inspector near Haramani Mandap, Cuttack;
(iii) The Organizer of the Mandap will also obtain NOC from Superintending Engineer, R & B,
regarding the sustainability and stability of the gate and thereafter permission from the Dy.
Commissioner of Police, Cuttack;
Md. Shahbaz, Superintending Engineer, R & B Division No.1, Cuttack appearing through virtual mode intimates this Court regarding structural safety of the gates before erection and during the course of erection and after completion, the same shall be monitored and only after being satisfied about its structural stability and safety, no objection certificate shall be issued.
(iv) The Organizer has been instructed that overhead construction of gate should not be done which may cause hindrance to immersion;
(v) The Puja Committee members should not erect any gate /pandal encroaching portion of land of other Sahi and Bustee which may invite law and order problem;
(vi) Each Puja Committee should have extinguisher in the pandal/mandap to avoid fire hazard;
(vii) The electric fitting should be made in Mandaps by authorized contractor.
A copy of the proceeding of preparatory meeting dated 18.08.2025 and agenda have been annexed to the letter as Annexure-A series.
However, it is brought to the notice of this Court that a peace committee meeting was held on 24.08.2025, chaired by Cuttack District Collector, Mr. Dattatraya Bhausaheb Shinde in which the District Administration discussed with the Puja Committee members regarding the arrangements to be made for smooth and peaceful conduct of Durga Puja and other festivals to be held thereafter in compliance of the directions issued by this Court dated 21.08.2025.

(iii) It is further stated in the compliance letter that the ACP DIB -cum- Licensing C e l l , C u t t a c k U P D h a s a l s o b e e n d i r e c t e d t o e n s u r e t h a t t h e instructions/guidelines/orders of the Court be followed strictly and also while granting the application for permission under section 4(2) of the ODISHA FIRE WORKS AND LOUD SPEAKERS (REGULATION) Act, 1958, THE ODISHA URBAN POLICE Act, 2003 and other relevant Acts;
(iv) It is further stated in the compliance letter that all IICs of Cuttack City have been directed to make awareness programmes in their respective P.Ss jurisdiction to sensitize the Secretary/President of different Puja Committee as well as general public not to play excessive noise/loud music during festive seasons in their respective Puja Mandaps, cultural programmes and immersion procession etc.,
because it causes negative effects on people and the environment.

(b) The Organizers of Puja Committee/ owners of sound speakers/sound systems/band parties shall not use any sound system beyond the prescribed limit i.e. 65 decibel at night between 10.00 p.m. to 6.00 a.m.;
(c) The Organizers/workers of Puja Committee shall not use any fireworks;
(d) Puja Mandaps including gates will be constructed without causing traffic congestion for vehicular and pedestrian traffic;
(e) No DJ will be allowed during puja and immersion;
(f) Licenses are being issued for use of loud speaker/mike under the provisions of Section-4 Orissa,
Fire Works and Loudspeakers Act, 1958 read with sections 28 and 29 of Orissa Urban Police Act,
2003 and Regulations 47 and 56 conditions including use of maximum 06 nos. of sound boxes to be put on the trolley during procession with 65 decibels;

Accordingly, letter of acceptance has been issued to all agencies for drawl of agreement covering different chainages of 15 numbers of arterial roads and ring road for which renewal coat of bitumen will be laid for smooth movement of traffic;
(ii) As per the said LOA, work will start by 1st week of September 2025 and it will be completed by 3rd week of September 2025 for Cuttack City Ring Road, Buxi Bazar area, Choudhary Bazar area,
Chandini Chowk, Dolomundai, Seminary Chhak, etc.

The list of all such roads for which tender has been invited has been annexed to the affidavit as Annexure-A;
