Mr. Baishnu Bhusan Behera, General Manager, WATCO Division, Cuttack who is present through virtual mode has filed an affidavit dated 25.08.2025, wherein it is stated as follows:
(i) WATCO will ensure uninterrupted and hygienic water supply during the festive season;
(ii) Additionally, PVC tanks and Water Tankers will be deployed at strategic locations as per requirement;
(iii) To ensure water quality disinfection through chlorine/bleaching powder at WTP made @ of 3-5 Mg./Ltr. intermediate storage reservoir @ 1-2 Mg./Ltr. and at consumer end @ 0.2-0.5/Mg/Ltr.

All the production wells are being disinfected through gravity dosing system;
(iv) The water supply pipe lines are being washed to clean the deposition of iron oxide;
(v) The quality of drinking water is being monitored on day to day basis by third party laboratory from source intermediate storage reservoir, consumer ends, stand posts, production well etc. as per schedule.

Every day (except Sunday) around 30-40 numbers samples in CMC area are collected and tested by the third party laboratory (M/s. Spectro Analytical Labs Ltd.);
(vi) The Field engineers and staff of WATCO are testing more than 20 samples per day for residual chlorine content at consumer end through field test kit, which are being recorded everyday;
(vii) The Jalasathis engaged by WATCO are also testing more than 50 water samples per day at consumer end through field test kit for residual chlorine;
(viii) The residual chlorine test made everyday by the field staff of WATCO and GPS photographs shared everyday in a joint whatsapp group of WATCO, CMC and Health Department official are recorded;
(ix) WATCO is trying its level best to supply safe & clean drinking water uninterruptedly during coming festival to the public, and also to prevent water borne diseases any more.
The said affidavit is taken on record.

